{
  "name": "HL·04 Dispatch",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## HL·04 Dispatch (lesson 6.4)\nCalled by HL·03 with {order_id}. Nearest free rider (zone table) → Telegram job with Accept, then Delivered → customer gets approved WhatsApp templates (the 24-hour window may have closed).\nOwns: deliveries, riders.free. Never writes orders (one owner per table); \"dispatched\"/\"delivered\" are events + deliveries rows.\n\nTables: riders(rider_id, name, telegram_chat_id, zone, free bool, last_job_at), deliveries(order_id pk, rider_id, assigned_at, accepted_at, delivered_at).\nTemplates (approved in Meta): out_for_delivery and delivered, each with one body variable = order_id.\n\n**Credentials:** Postgres, Telegram (rider bot), WhatsApp (HTTP). **Replace:** YOUR_WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID, YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "41dca868-6aac-44d1-9573-450cfad54aa7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -528,
        -324
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "04145955-59f4-4374-9b5c-16b5bae64ed5",
      "name": "From HL·03",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT o.order_id, o.items, o.total_ngn, c.wa_phone, c.name, c.zone\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.order_id = $1;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [ $json.order_id ] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "706cb547-adef-4cc5-bf48-42fe88f4bb96",
      "name": "Get order and customer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "WITH r AS (\n  SELECT rider_id FROM riders\n  WHERE free\n  ORDER BY (zone = $2) DESC, last_job_at NULLS FIRST\n  LIMIT 1 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\n), upd AS (\n  UPDATE riders SET free = false, last_job_at = now() FROM r\n  WHERE riders.rider_id = r.rider_id\n  RETURNING riders.rider_id, riders.name, riders.telegram_chat_id\n), d AS (\n  INSERT INTO deliveries (order_id, rider_id, assigned_at)\n  SELECT $1, rider_id, now() FROM upd\n  ON CONFLICT (order_id) DO UPDATE SET rider_id = EXCLUDED.rider_id, assigned_at = now()\n)\nSELECT * FROM upd;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [ $json.order_id, $json.zone ] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "5f96a8bf-4f1f-4d29-b17e-c59a9d9452b8",
      "name": "Assign nearest free rider",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "6d290437-4d32-4617-a046-ac41c7fb4216",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.rider_id ?? '' }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a2c9f3f-e16c-4fba-b3dd-4decc89607bb",
      "name": "Rider found?",
